<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <h1 id="page-title">Cat FAQ</h1>
      <p class="lead">A cozy collection of common cat questions, with each answer tucked away until you want it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
      <div class="example">
        <h2 class="question">
          <button type="button" class="toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1" id="question-1">
            <span>Why do cats purr?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-1">
          <p>Cats purr for comfort, communication, and sometimes self-soothing. A purr can mean “I’m happy,” but it can also show up when a cat is stressed or healing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2 class="question">
          <button type="button" class="toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
            <span>Do cats really land on their feet?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-2">
          <p>They often do, thanks to a flexible spine, a fast righting reflex, and a body built to twist mid-air. That said, falls can still injure cats, so windows and balconies should be secured.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2 class="question">
          <button type="button" class="toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
            <span>Why do cats knead blankets and laps?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-3">
          <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats may knead when they feel relaxed, safe, or especially fond of the person or spot beneath their paws.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2 class="question">
          <button type="button" class="toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
            <span>How much do cats sleep?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-4">
          <p>Many cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day, and some sleep even more. They tend to save energy for bursts of play, hunting instincts, and exploratory zoomies.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    document.documentElement.classList.add('js');

    document.querySelectorAll('.example').forEach((item) => {
      const button = item.querySelector('.toggle');
      const panel = item.querySelector('.details');

      panel.hidden = true;

      const setExpanded = (expanded) => {
        button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(expanded));
        panel.hidden = !expanded;
      };

      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const isExpanded = button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
        setExpanded(!isExpanded);
      });

      item.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
        if (event.key !== 'Escape') {
          return;
        }

        if (button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true') {
          setExpanded(false);
          button.focus();
        }
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
